-- title:
--   Actual original-source discounted stopped finite-band compensated jump Taylor term has L1 norm bounded by physical finite-band L2 energy
-- statement:
--   For original spectrally negative Levy X and dividends D with inclusive ruin stopping and discount horizon, every literal compensated finite-band Taylor jump integral Jn is P-integrable with ordinary P-L1 absolute size at most the physical predictable L2 square-energy norm of the truncated kernel. The original source representation hSource remains an explicit hypothesis, without assuming finite small-jump first moment.
-- source:
--   Use hSource n to identify the literal compensated jump band with the isometric Lp2(P) image F of the truncated original GW. The probability Lp comparison eLpNorm1≤eLpNorm2 and integral_norm_eq_lintegral_enorm bound the absolute P integral by ‖F‖. Source isometry hIso and Lp.norm_toLp identify that norm with the physical product square-energy eLpNorm2 of the truncated kernel.

